#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d3c239f-a333-5d88-ae92-08380d731a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d3c239f-a333-5d88-ae92-08380d731a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e8eaf8-51e0-5844-8acf-f4e6db888966" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4dcc068-e785-52f8-bc25-d5e3ae981a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4dcc068-e785-52f8-bc25-d5e3ae981a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303493} :answer-field/id #uuid "330de255-3b94-5b56-9e5a-f8f0c53758db" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1dba81c8-6f48-528d-b583-abc4c231bef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-282260" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2x,0,4⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{280}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$"}]}
